<p>No other Indian spice export concentrates this heavily in one region. Calendar 2024 data shows the UAE (USD 80.5 million) and Saudi Arabia (USD 43.1 million) together accounting for roughly 61% of India's total USD 203.6 million cardamom exports — and adding Kuwait, Iraq and Oman pushes Gulf markets above 70% of total export value. The demand is cultural: cardamom is essential rather than optional in qahwa, traditional Arabic coffee, and runs through a range of traditional dishes and desserts. That supports pricing few other spice markets match — roughly USD 22.5 per kg average export value, by a wide margin the highest unit-value spice India exports, against a total 2024 volume of just 9,033 MT. This guide is for UAE, Saudi and wider GCC buyers building a spice-sourcing programme around that demand.</p>

<!-- slot:facts -->

